{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/pack.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.312388Z","id":"b6fd71584420459e52737e0caaab14c4bed771850448e73df1441e98f0ef0f29","body":{"detail":"ParsedPack::parse keeps each entry's inflated bytes and resolve() builds a second map of resolved objects, so a push needs roughly two to three times its inflated size in memory; resolve() repeats a pass over every unresolved entry until none resolves, so a chain of length L costs L passes. With ServeOptions::max_push_bytes at 64 MiB (crates/clax-git/src/server.rs) a Durable Object (128 MB) can run out of memory on a large push. Fix: resolve each delta from its base by offset with a dependency order (bases first) and drop entries as they are written, or lower the push limit for the Worker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"668a4707154c257db51fc6e9a52ba7060509c2b2c850c360bf4c304f562dc596"},"summary":"Reading a pushed pack holds every entry inflated and every resolved object at once, and resolves delta chains in rounds over all entries","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/memory.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.313282Z","id":"4e7536f7cf46880195abb7bfb8f1ade52cb24384b8d455944ef3658c2abe80c0","body":{"detail":"Repo::apply writes objects before it compares and swaps refs (crates/clax-git/src/repo.rs documents this), so a publish refused for a stale parent or a push refused as non-fast-forward leaves its blobs, trees and commit in MemoryHost; RepoHost::delete drops only the refs and the held set. Harmless for tests and a local stand-in; a long-running stand-in grows. Fix: write objects only when an update applies, and drop objects no repository holds on delete.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"1dbfdecf886a4140a24a33a44cefdfea22b86579ea9c65b847c8fe11e98bf6c6"},"summary":"MemoryRepo::apply stores the objects of a refused update, and deleting a repository keeps its objects","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.313552Z","id":"920746d7a42e1d70c7a8c2ed7b637c218e262874b13d84785fef2a23d4578dc9","body":{"detail":"unpack() resolves the pack and links() parses each commit, tree and tag, and check_update() walks connectivity, but a pushed tree with an entry named .git, .., a duplicate name, unsorted entries or a bad mode is accepted and later served; git clients refuse such trees on checkout and git fsck --strict reports them. Fix: check trees as git fsck does (entry order, names, modes) and commits' header order before applying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1062},"end":{"line":1064},"content_hash":"53e9d55b2afa702632962f7e6f5159e13fd9e3bc729f5ea821d49c0336f2daac"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks that pushed objects parse and connect, not what git's receive.fsckObjects checks","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.313717Z","id":"f9cd295fa13180e34d6161caafe8cd72160285badac19b3f360418797fac78bb","body":{"detail":"ReceiveOptions::deny_non_fast_forwards defaults to true so main only appends, matching versions as one commit per publish. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts refuses force pushes is not known here; the hosted prototype's memory store refused every push (hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts). If Artifacts accepts them, the stand-in should too, and recording versions from a push must handle a rewritten main (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcile).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"6033d380035b54a1bc3e4cbf3f04994f23aae8c10c39e5fc961d3f7e14edcf1d"},"summary":"Allow non-fast-forward pushes to refs/heads/* in the stand-in server","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.313862Z","id":"f7f856c0ee767896292b1b48c64e6f7038a987fcf093ee0655b67987a9d62286","body":{"detail":"GitVersions reads parent commits and log entries by parsing raw commit objects (crates/clax-git/src/versions.rs read_commit), and PushingRepo reads through an ObjectReader that answers raw objects. The hosted prototype's binding answers readCommit as metadata (hosted/src/repo/artifacts.ts: ArtifactsCommitMetadata), readTree as entries and readBlob as bytes, so trees and blobs re-encode exactly but a commit's raw bytes (and so its ID) cannot be rebuilt reliably. Options: re-encode commits from metadata and check the ID against the hash; fetch objects over upload-pack (a client this crate does not have yet); or give GitVersions a commit-metadata read path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"f4cab2018c684c3b3b635b1f9f9fb1dd0750392f2cd8f55482b4d4c588d1e5a8"},"summary":"A Cloudflare Artifacts Repo needs raw git objects, which the ARTIFACTS binding does not hand out for commits","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.314050Z","id":"29acab7b594e2ff83ce59b6cea15d4c32dbd80ded58412dc7a6db342795cbb06","body":{"detail":"negotiate() collects every object the wants reach (less the common history) and write_pack() stores each whole, as hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts did; a clone of an artifact with many versions of big files sends each version of each file in full and holds the pack in memory. Fix: stream the pack and deltify file versions against their previous version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":676},"end":{"line":676},"content_hash":"67ec5301494261c28c07a0d46438468e35e445e6089f68906aa1fb03ec01e3eb"},"summary":"Upload-pack builds the whole pack in memory, undeltified, for every clone and fetch","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:44:02.314347Z","id":"d5c0c8a4831220b7469ee73206425b0332f7f9009bd04412d87b82df1e576ccd","body":{"detail":"Not here: hosted/src/git/commands.ts (clone_command and jj_clone_command strings), hosted/src/git/tokens.ts (minting git tokens), hosted/src/repo/content-type.ts, hosted/src/repo/artifacts.ts (ArtifactsRepoStore: binding calls, write-token caching and the retry on a 401/403, which GitError::Auth is for), and recording pushed commits as versions (recordPushes in hosted/src/do/artifact.ts; GitVersions::log gives the first-parent chain it walks). Wiring into clax-core and clax-server is not done either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"36c03e0024f4f2c6d7a164e32e250bef32f3e78cf62c4ef4dcf72828655a6bc8"},"summary":"Parts of the hosted prototype's git layer are not ported to this crate","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/pack.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.547327Z","id":"ff07a585d1ac7ce6125bd89d57eb1f080fffcdfdbffa227213c00d0b07c7756a","body":{"detail":"ParsedPack::parse_bounded keeps each entry's inflated bytes, and resolve() copies each whole entry and adds every object a delta makes, so a push needs up to about twice max_unpacked_bytes (1 GiB by default, DEFAULT_MAX_UNPACKED_BYTES in crates/clax-git/src/pack.rs). A Durable Object has 128 MB. Delta chains now resolve in one pass from a worklist (the rounds over every entry are gone). Fix: drop entries as they are resolved and written, or set max_unpacked_bytes (and max_push_bytes) to what the Worker holds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":268},"end":{"line":278},"content_hash":"1e1e7b8ddcf822a1614fcaf697bf61f903c4933bef9f14d5701f22779d241500"},"summary":"Reading a pushed pack holds every entry inflated and every resolved object at once, up to about twice ReceiveOptions::max_unpacked_bytes","supersedes":"b6fd71584420459e52737e0caaab14c4bed771850448e73df1441e98f0ef0f29","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/memory.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.549487Z","id":"19f6f610593a2f858acfd6c690300eb7ce5d0f2ef57acf44695e6e0d7984dc20","body":{"detail":"Repo::apply writes objects before it compares and swaps refs (crates/clax-git/src/repo.rs documents this), so a publish refused for a stale parent or a push refused as non-fast-forward leaves its blobs, trees and commit in MemoryHost; RepoHost::delete drops only the refs and the held set. Harmless for tests and a local stand-in; a long-running stand-in grows. Fix: write objects only when an update applies, and drop objects no repository holds on delete.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"1dbfdecf886a4140a24a33a44cefdfea22b86579ea9c65b847c8fe11e98bf6c6"},"summary":"MemoryRepo::apply stores the objects of a refused update, and deleting a repository keeps its objects","supersedes":"4e7536f7cf46880195abb7bfb8f1ade52cb24384b8d455944ef3658c2abe80c0","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.551016Z","id":"e44d747e79e66a9d2c094c5b50f949338799b79d71d122ff952db7709d25208d","body":{"detail":"ReceiveOptions::deny_non_fast_forwards defaults to true so main only appends, matching versions as one commit per publish. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts refuses force pushes is not known here; the hosted prototype's memory store refused every push (hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts). If Artifacts accepts them, the stand-in should too, and recording versions from a push must handle a rewritten main (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcile).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"0988b2a35405c5f46a9e656263d98f5680e98cdfac14012b88d649f8232d99e2"},"summary":"Allow non-fast-forward pushes to refs/heads/* in the stand-in server","supersedes":"f9cd295fa13180e34d6161caafe8cd72160285badac19b3f360418797fac78bb","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.552567Z","id":"cccaf595b42fc6b6b6c0d86997724f26e395935cc933a88a779f15b2c07f5ec2","body":{"detail":"negotiate() collects every object the wants reach (less the common history) and write_pack() stores each whole, as hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts did; a clone of an artifact with many versions of big files sends each version of each file in full and holds the pack in memory. Fix: stream the pack and deltify file versions against their previous version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":713},"end":{"line":713},"content_hash":"67ec5301494261c28c07a0d46438468e35e445e6089f68906aa1fb03ec01e3eb"},"summary":"Upload-pack builds the whole pack in memory, undeltified, for every clone and fetch","supersedes":"29acab7b594e2ff83ce59b6cea15d4c32dbd80ded58412dc7a6db342795cbb06","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.554015Z","id":"424ec84c778a93e4087263a2c3b692929307c7c91c3b1e6a9fd87aea2682bc92","body":{"detail":"unpack() resolves the pack and links() parses each commit, tree and tag; unconnected() walks what a new ref value reaches and checks each link's type (a commit's tree a tree, its parents commits, a tree entry what its mode says, a tag's target its declared type). A pushed tree with an entry named .git, .., a duplicate name, unsorted entries, a non-UTF-8 name or a bad mode is still accepted and later served; git clients refuse such trees on checkout and git fsck --strict reports them. Fix: check trees as git fsck does (entry order, names, modes) and commits' header order before applying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":888},"end":{"line":957},"content_hash":"a64a619f7ee4e4383e300fb9c3d8d514e2ebed35ee96f0e626d09b6dfe44cc45"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks that pushed objects parse, connect and have the type that names them, not the rest of what git's receive.fsckObjects checks","supersedes":"920746d7a42e1d70c7a8c2ed7b637c218e262874b13d84785fef2a23d4578dc9","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555501Z","id":"4c8a2ed143f7f36ce9c91174cec873f1fba8dccaace8a527285c77bb30fcf4bd","body":{"detail":"check_update applies the fast-forward rule to refs/heads/* only; an update of refs/tags/* needs only connectivity, and ReceiveOptions::deny_deletes is false by default. Over a MemoryRepo with main at c2 and refs/tags/v1 at c1, receive_pack of `<c1> <c2> refs/tags/v1` answers `ok refs/tags/v1`, and then `<c2> 0000… refs/tags/v1` answers `ok refs/tags/v1`. GitVersions::read_file(Rev::Version(1)) then reads another commit than the version clax-core recorded, and a pusher who creates refs/tags/v<n+1> first makes the next publish fail (`refs/tags/v<n+1> already exists`). Options: refuse creating, moving and deleting refs/tags/v<n> by push in the stand-in (version tags are written by GitVersions only); or accept them and have the push reconcile treat clax-core's store as authoritative and restore the tags. Which one also depends on what Cloudflare Artifacts allows (record f9cd295f on this file).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1168},"end":{"line":1214},"content_hash":"e0f7a381180de9ad8881fd7f66c808af747d0956888e34b3fa6b97c82f403cbe"},"summary":"A push may move or delete any tag, the version tags v<n> included","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555555Z","id":"de68c643ee5a17bbdd8280d1d0f5fa8439e84966a215dcf39f9c77bdc71644ce","body":{"detail":"receive() calls check_update for every command, and each call's unconnected() walks the pushed objects again with a fresh seen set, and a non-fast-forward check walks history from the new value. The command count is bounded only by max_push_bytes (64 MiB holds about 600 000 command lines), so one push with a Write token can take commands × objects work. Fix: share one set of objects already found connected across the updates, and cap the number of commands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1084},"end":{"line":1086},"content_hash":"670280c48be1416785b16e364eae7343c00f3d81fab1ba939624b0cbae7377a5"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks each ref update separately, so a push of many commands costs commands times pushed objects","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/object.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555609Z","id":"4ee67e554837e14bbe3f96f31f3e35368d5f627f6c64cf1fd5491733913f9cdd","body":{"detail":"TreeEntry::name is a String and parse_tree decodes names with from_utf8_lossy. build_tree (crates/clax-git/src/tree.rs) re-encodes the parent's entries, so a publish on top of a tree holding a name of byte 0xff (pushable to the stand-in, which accepts any name) writes that entry as U+FFFD: over a MemoryRepo holding such a tree, build_tree with a change to `g` answers a root tree with the bytes EF BF BD in place of FF. Two such names decode to one key in build()'s BTreeMap, so one of them is dropped. Fix: keep names as bytes in TreeEntry, or refuse non-UTF-8 names at receive-pack (record 920746d7's tree checks).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"0776a1bbb7c815a3ae7c52353b8032363d9283f11c833091905e4d2e01fcc33f"},"summary":"parse_tree reads entry names lossily, so building a tree on one with a non-UTF-8 name renames that entry","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/object.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555643Z","id":"ad3c5b2fec5d4e933a69c9dd84777b6f911e858f32407c0665f1148118002622","body":{"detail":"Signature::format refuses `<`, `>`, a newline or NUL in a name or email (invalid_argument), and GitVersions::publish and fork write VersionMeta::author as given. The hosted prototype passes the person's display name unchanged (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts:1485), so a name such as `Rae <3` makes every publish of that person fail. git itself drops these characters from an ident (strbuf_addstr_without_crud in ident.c). Fix: strip them from the name, as git does, keeping the refusal for the email, which Clax builds from the person ID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":265},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"637e01de97de2fcf9298458d71b11dbc0cfd482b051da37e199d4aebe58d33a0"},"summary":"A publisher whose display name holds < or > cannot publish: the commit author is refused","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/versions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555872Z","id":"33d5a56e89213701eb10cc5c9660d127f41414777d2508fd0a89fe78428939a7","body":{"detail":"GitVersions::fork calls RepoHost::fork, then deletes the copied version tags, then commits v1; when the tag deletion or commit_refs fails, repository a-<to> stays with the source's history and no v1, and a second fork to the same artifact answers `Repository a-<to> already exists`. Fix: delete `to` when a step after the copy fails (best effort), or let fork resume into an existing copy that has no v1.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":376},"content_hash":"8ccbc47d3fe670c95416ce24a4b5ee9137f6ccc3d0a24115bcb6bdbabeb5e6b8"},"summary":"A fork that fails after copying the repository leaves the copy, and the retry is refused","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.555945Z","id":"f02a5f692b60c927a80e06758a0cbefff4a0f248b5f2fa06429742ba6e59e99e","body":{"detail":"Every `<id> <name>` line becomes a ref, so a remote that advertises alternates (`<id> .have`, which git's receive-pack sends for a repository with alternates) answers a ref named `.have` from PushingRepo::refs; a `shallow <id>` line fails ObjectId::from_hex on `shallow` and the whole advertisement is refused as malformed. Fix: keep HEAD and names under refs/, and skip other lines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"449b39bb01a3cefade46c294ec41e98e72ed3084dbbd6839154ef097d0e0b797"},"summary":"parse_advertisement keeps `.have` lines as a ref and refuses an advertisement with `shallow` lines","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/tree.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.556115Z","id":"23eb1a7bde9f7216f2a229b3813003e5109bce847c726e8fda1d2989eaf4dabc","body":{"detail":"git's verify_path, with core.protectHFS and core.protectNTFS (on by default on macOS and Windows), refuses to check out a path whose segment is .git with Unicode characters HFS+ ignores (`.g\\u200cit`), the 8.3 name `git~1`, or .git with trailing dots or spaces (`.git.`, `.git `). path_segments accepts these, so a publish holding such a path is taken and a clone on those systems fails at checkout. Fix: refuse them as git's is_hfs_dotgit and is_ntfs_dotgit do.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"de17817047986abbcdf3f91c34c13f702d36e61afdd671b60986d6f2ddfd2b2a"},"summary":"path_segments refuses .git in any case but not the names git treats as .git on macOS and Windows","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:12:42.556234Z","id":"9b2a74fcded82737bb5a203dbb0f88829ac4dc8f1bf934f4fd99ecaab6136a1b","body":{"detail":"What GitVersions reads from a commit is its tree, parents, message (trailers) and signatures: publish needs the parent's tree (versions.rs publish), read_file and list_files the version's tree, fork the source commit's tree, log the first-parent chain with messages. None needs the commit's raw bytes or recomputes its ID; the commit IDs come from refs. The binding's metadata carries exactly these. Re-encoding from metadata and checking the hash fails for commits people push (gpgsig, encoding, extra headers, other time zones), which are the ones the push reconcile reads. An upload-pack client is a negotiation plus a full pack per read from a Durable Object, for data the binding already answers. Since clax-core's store already holds each version's number, publisher and note, the git side is only the content and history. Shape: a Repo method such as read_commit_meta(id) -> Option<CommitMeta> whose default parses read_object (MemoryRepo and the stand-in keep working), overridden by the Artifacts repository from readCommit; GitVersions and tree.rs use it and read_object only for trees and blobs. The receive-pack client never sends a parent commit, so pushes are unaffected. This is needed before the Artifacts wiring, not before this crate merges.","kind":"comment","references":"f7f856c0ee767896292b1b48c64e6f7038a987fcf093ee0655b67987a9d62286","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"f4cab2018c684c3b3b635b1f9f9fb1dd0750392f2cd8f55482b4d4c588d1e5a8"},"summary":"Recommendation: give GitVersions a commit-metadata read path; neither re-encode commits nor fetch over upload-pack","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.446570Z","id":"44d9aaf7fef00aee461768e0f10ca84f183adfe36f1e1fb12332080f1bb9de64","body":{"detail":"check_update (crates/clax-git/src/server.rs, the protect_version_tags check) answers `ng <ref> refs/tags/v* are Clax's version tags` for any ref starting refs/tags/v, before connectivity; ReceiveOptions::protect_version_tags defaults to true. Version tags are written only through Repo::apply (GitVersions, clax-content-git's GitContent), which receive-pack does not go through. Test over real git push: tests/smart_http.rs refuses_a_push_that_creates_moves_or_deletes_a_version_tag (create v3, force-move v1, delete v1, and an atomic push of main plus v3 are all refused with refs unchanged; main plus tag x1 is taken). What is left is recorded separately on the same check: the prefix also refuses tags such as v1.0, and the refusal exists only where Clax serves receive-pack.","kind":"comment","references":"4c8a2ed143f7f36ce9c91174cec873f1fba8dccaace8a527285c77bb30fcf4bd","summary":"Decision implemented: Clax owns the v<n> tags, so receive-pack refuses every pushed update (create, move, delete) of a ref under refs/tags/v","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.446849Z","id":"e9072a445f41fd25483facba97b097368cf56b30278484996fa477e91585156a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:547dfd6b","summary":"Fixed: receive-pack refuses pushes that create, move or delete refs/tags/v*. `cargo test -p clax-git refuses_a_push_that_creates_moves_or_deletes_a_version_tag`: test smart_http::refuses_a_push_that_creates_moves_or_deletes_a_version_tag ... ok","supersedes":"4c8a2ed143f7f36ce9c91174cec873f1fba8dccaace8a527285c77bb30fcf4bd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.454054Z","id":"ffe0400cc0970089cf32c205a2f4d25b00d5d1d9517963d461d45d579d3d955b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-git/src/repo.rs: CommitMeta moved there (re-exported from versions), Repo::read_commit_meta and ObjectReader::read_commit_meta with defaults that parse read_object; PushingRepo forwards to its reader, so an Artifacts reader overrides ObjectReader::read_commit_meta from the binding's readCommit. GitVersions (publish, fork, read_file, list_files, log, set_tags, commit_of_repo) and clax-content-git read commits only through it; raw objects remain for trees, blobs, annotated tags (commit_of_repo peels them with read_object) and the server's upload-pack and receive-pack checks. Test: tests/versions.rs versions_read_commits_through_the_metadata_path, over a host whose read_object has no commits.","kind":"comment","references":"f7f856c0ee767896292b1b48c64e6f7038a987fcf093ee0655b67987a9d62286","summary":"Decision implemented: commits are read through Repo::read_commit_meta, defaulting to parsing the raw object and overridable by a repository that answers commits as metadata","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.454286Z","id":"60fcde26a5ed16b5cd4f2e6694ba78eb296d0a7ca862c21d04471572dee7ff19","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:107a27c9","summary":"Fixed: Repo::read_commit_meta is the commit read path. `cargo test -p clax-git versions_read_commits_through_the_metadata_path`: test versions::versions_read_commits_through_the_metadata_path ... ok","supersedes":"f7f856c0ee767896292b1b48c64e6f7038a987fcf093ee0655b67987a9d62286","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/versions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.473890Z","id":"de3bd28f5f1a7dafe4731bb1496a816af811cf532fa30b5e01989801b852a833","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs fork; the contract check contract::a_fork_makes_version_one_of_a_new_artifact retries a failed fork. GitVersions::fork itself is unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"33d5a56e89213701eb10cc5c9660d127f41414777d2508fd0a89fe78428939a7","summary":"clax-content-git's GitContent::fork does not have this: it deletes the copy when any step after RepoHost::fork fails, and deletes an existing target repository that holds no version tag before forking","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.474415Z","id":"14e3dd87b7f5a8a56c02b26cffdc5ac4d52a027acecc85c8544b268b71069214","body":{"detail":"The check refuses every ref starting refs/tags/v, so a pusher's own tags v1.0 or vendor-x are refused along with v<n>; version_of_tag_ref (versions.rs) would narrow it to v<digits>. And it runs only in this crate's server (the local stand-in): a push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts' git endpoint is checked by Artifacts, whose tag rules are not known here, so a pushed v<n+1> there makes the next write of n+1 fail (refs/tags/v<n+1> already exists) and a moved v<n> changes what version n reads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1201},"content_hash":"a671034c0123cad77f0624b267b3f1dd28fc80ea2833e5b97994166e6ebca4b3"},"summary":"Version tags are protected by prefix, and only where Clax serves receive-pack","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' ref and tag rules are known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.483213Z","id":"ffa0ae0b1f48f5e2ec9953a905e97f99ee1f049b83c5facc47a5852fcd45ee84","body":{"detail":"Every `<id> <name>` line becomes a ref, so a remote that advertises alternates (`<id> .have`, which git's receive-pack sends for a repository with alternates) answers a ref named `.have` from PushingRepo::refs; a `shallow <id>` line fails ObjectId::from_hex on `shallow` and the whole advertisement is refused as malformed. Fix: keep HEAD and names under refs/, and skip other lines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"449b39bb01a3cefade46c294ec41e98e72ed3084dbbd6839154ef097d0e0b797"},"summary":"parse_advertisement keeps `.have` lines as a ref and refuses an advertisement with `shallow` lines","supersedes":"f02a5f692b60c927a80e06758a0cbefff4a0f248b5f2fa06429742ba6e59e99e","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.488856Z","id":"ce995d14d1602576dbe9688b7beea116632367486f240599e74c301b82c89c1a","body":{"detail":"Not here: hosted/src/git/commands.ts (clone_command and jj_clone_command strings), hosted/src/git/tokens.ts (minting git tokens), hosted/src/repo/content-type.ts, hosted/src/repo/artifacts.ts (ArtifactsRepoStore: binding calls, write-token caching and the retry on a 401/403, which GitError::Auth is for), and recording pushed commits as versions (recordPushes in hosted/src/do/artifact.ts; GitVersions::log gives the first-parent chain it walks). Wiring into clax-core and clax-server is not done either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"ea4ffb1d2f0b82d5c1208abee11ba04466af795ef3b92625f555a582487bc7e4"},"summary":"Parts of the hosted prototype's git layer are not ported to this crate","supersedes":"d5c0c8a4831220b7469ee73206425b0332f7f9009bd04412d87b82df1e576ccd","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.490767Z","id":"7b1fc80c774a6fd9626883ee720323b8adf5aa2e19bb79b415d8d9ba284ab550","body":{"detail":"ReceiveOptions::deny_non_fast_forwards defaults to true so main only appends, matching versions as one commit per publish. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts refuses force pushes is not known here; the hosted prototype's memory store refused every push (hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts). If Artifacts accepts them, the stand-in should too, and recording versions from a push must handle a rewritten main (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcile).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"a0923519c945e4221d9854a7f2a395588c2dab44fde9440df0abea0c4e2f46f3"},"summary":"Allow non-fast-forward pushes to refs/heads/* in the stand-in server","supersedes":"e44d747e79e66a9d2c094c5b50f949338799b79d71d122ff952db7709d25208d","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.492473Z","id":"f78ceef0e430a587f087adebd8f4faa86d62741a74172771274be36334d9dd54","body":{"detail":"negotiate() collects every object the wants reach (less the common history) and write_pack() stores each whole, as hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts did; a clone of an artifact with many versions of big files sends each version of each file in full and holds the pack in memory. Fix: stream the pack and deltify file versions against their previous version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":729},"end":{"line":729},"content_hash":"67ec5301494261c28c07a0d46438468e35e445e6089f68906aa1fb03ec01e3eb"},"summary":"Upload-pack builds the whole pack in memory, undeltified, for every clone and fetch","supersedes":"cccaf595b42fc6b6b6c0d86997724f26e395935cc933a88a779f15b2c07f5ec2","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.494190Z","id":"30c0f5f16b041ad6d214d1a20976d7df0d8819c22e91a6301c2ea6fea560f0e1","body":{"detail":"unpack() resolves the pack and links() parses each commit, tree and tag; unconnected() walks what a new ref value reaches and checks each link's type (a commit's tree a tree, its parents commits, a tree entry what its mode says, a tag's target its declared type). A pushed tree with an entry named .git, .., a duplicate name, unsorted entries, a non-UTF-8 name or a bad mode is still accepted and later served; git clients refuse such trees on checkout and git fsck --strict reports them. Fix: check trees as git fsck does (entry order, names, modes) and commits' header order before applying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":904},"end":{"line":973},"content_hash":"a64a619f7ee4e4383e300fb9c3d8d514e2ebed35ee96f0e626d09b6dfe44cc45"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks that pushed objects parse, connect and have the type that names them, not the rest of what git's receive.fsckObjects checks","supersedes":"424ec84c778a93e4087263a2c3b692929307c7c91c3b1e6a9fd87aea2682bc92","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.495868Z","id":"aced13ef33ab9c653c73cdeee9ca42ca7d6dce5af7cc9b90e7d20be36fe164fb","body":{"detail":"receive() calls check_update for every command, and each call's unconnected() walks the pushed objects again with a fresh seen set, and a non-fast-forward check walks history from the new value. The command count is bounded only by max_push_bytes (64 MiB holds about 600 000 command lines), so one push with a Write token can take commands × objects work. Fix: share one set of objects already found connected across the updates, and cap the number of commands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1100},"end":{"line":1102},"content_hash":"670280c48be1416785b16e364eae7343c00f3d81fab1ba939624b0cbae7377a5"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks each ref update separately, so a push of many commands costs commands times pushed objects","supersedes":"de68c643ee5a17bbdd8280d1d0f5fa8439e84966a215dcf39f9c77bdc71644ce","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/versions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:05:54.499525Z","id":"bed249c9ed40921d9cbf9a371a289d10f2bce2dd1bb49325cf3c20fabd63d9a5","body":{"detail":"GitVersions::fork calls RepoHost::fork, then deletes the copied version tags, then commits v1; when the tag deletion or commit_refs fails, repository a-<to> stays with the source's history and no v1, and a second fork to the same artifact answers `Repository a-<to> already exists`. Fix: delete `to` when a step after the copy fails (best effort), or let fork resume into an existing copy that has no v1.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":273},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"8ccbc47d3fe670c95416ce24a4b5ee9137f6ccc3d0a24115bcb6bdbabeb5e6b8"},"summary":"A fork that fails after copying the repository leaves the copy, and the retry is refused","supersedes":"33d5a56e89213701eb10cc5c9660d127f41414777d2508fd0a89fe78428939a7","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.821108Z","id":"5846ac6a226ffa40aa13afff0f320bcbeba47f551ae02203dc426ce7f2b4fc2e","body":{"detail":"ReceiveOptions::deny_non_fast_forwards defaults to true so main only appends, matching versions as one commit per publish. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts refuses force pushes is not known here; the hosted prototype's memory store refused every push (hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts). If Artifacts accepts them, the stand-in should too, and recording versions from a push must handle a rewritten main (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcile).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"03ade68741271f2afc89c5f899f3f8f42328b95296e9daf2483138aa91fe7f34"},"summary":"Allow non-fast-forward pushes to refs/heads/* in the stand-in server","supersedes":"7b1fc80c774a6fd9626883ee720323b8adf5aa2e19bb79b415d8d9ba284ab550","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.822997Z","id":"db4094c473ff8b01b79c07c7ac1d64a2424781fe1d3a5051ceef6aba462df6a8","body":{"detail":"negotiate() collects every object the wants reach (less the common history) and write_pack() stores each whole, as hosted/src/git/upload-pack.ts did; a clone of an artifact with many versions of big files sends each version of each file in full and holds the pack in memory. Fix: stream the pack and deltify file versions against their previous version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":739},"end":{"line":739},"content_hash":"67ec5301494261c28c07a0d46438468e35e445e6089f68906aa1fb03ec01e3eb"},"summary":"Upload-pack builds the whole pack in memory, undeltified, for every clone and fetch","supersedes":"f78ceef0e430a587f087adebd8f4faa86d62741a74172771274be36334d9dd54","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.824757Z","id":"4ab81386db0b817ecab623392f37a6f1be2d6050d31b6bd375e04f0c87e29641","body":{"detail":"unpack() resolves the pack and links() parses each commit, tree and tag; unconnected() walks what a new ref value reaches and checks each link's type (a commit's tree a tree, its parents commits, a tree entry what its mode says, a tag's target its declared type). A pushed tree with an entry named .git, .., a duplicate name, unsorted entries, a non-UTF-8 name or a bad mode is still accepted and later served; git clients refuse such trees on checkout and git fsck --strict reports them. Fix: check trees as git fsck does (entry order, names, modes) and commits' header order before applying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":914},"end":{"line":983},"content_hash":"a64a619f7ee4e4383e300fb9c3d8d514e2ebed35ee96f0e626d09b6dfe44cc45"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks that pushed objects parse, connect and have the type that names them, not the rest of what git's receive.fsckObjects checks","supersedes":"30c0f5f16b041ad6d214d1a20976d7df0d8819c22e91a6301c2ea6fea560f0e1","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.826597Z","id":"fa7bce3cd41f03f086af0c3ddb22886aadb9c11c507ceaa3c04dfc5a4c4e0b82","body":{"detail":"receive() calls check_update for every command, and each call's unconnected() walks the pushed objects again with a fresh seen set, and a non-fast-forward check walks history from the new value. The command count is bounded only by max_push_bytes (64 MiB holds about 600 000 command lines), so one push with a Write token can take commands × objects work. Fix: share one set of objects already found connected across the updates, and cap the number of commands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1110},"end":{"line":1112},"content_hash":"670280c48be1416785b16e364eae7343c00f3d81fab1ba939624b0cbae7377a5"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks each ref update separately, so a push of many commands costs commands times pushed objects","supersedes":"aced13ef33ab9c653c73cdeee9ca42ca7d6dce5af7cc9b90e7d20be36fe164fb","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.832678Z","id":"6ff810dc09b9abec69aeb1697f695546e8a81b3434425be44c091b6bd4725e29","body":{"detail":"Since 416241a7 the check refuses exactly refs/tags/v<digits> (server::is_version_tag, server.rs:69), so a pusher's own v1.0 or vendor tags are taken (tests/smart_http.rs refuses_a_push_that_creates_moves_or_deletes_a_version_tag). It runs only in this crate's server (the local stand-in): a push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts' git endpoint is checked by Artifacts, whose tag rules are not known here, so a pushed v<n+1> there makes the next write of n+1 fail (refs/tags/v<n+1> already exists) and a moved v<n> changes what version n reads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1209},"end":{"line":1211},"content_hash":"743675678b02e7d2c03057d173640e16c5db38ebffaf08c8d21137e03df8d5d5"},"summary":"Version tags are protected only where Clax serves receive-pack","supersedes":"14e3dd87b7f5a8a56c02b26cffdc5ac4d52a027acecc85c8544b268b71069214","tags":["revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' ref and tag rules are known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/object.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.836984Z","id":"26730afd2a25de4e6ac91d6f7a62a3e85e8b73e1cf4c2360787c5402bab21494","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ad3c5b2fec5d4e933a69c9dd84777b6f911e858f32407c0665f1148118002622","summary":"clax-content-git's GitContent strips <, > and control characters from the publisher's name and the agent name before committing (ident_part, crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs:168; tests/with_git.rs git_log_shows_who_published_each_version_and_the_note commits as 'Rae 3' for 'Rae <3'). GitVersions::publish and fork here still refuse such a name.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/versions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:38:24.032170Z","id":"dff4ab0a844ac1ee6f872f32d1f8c00bd93a3ba4faa8a5b164d7667678e72ee5","body":{"detail":"GitVersions::fork calls versions::fork_at (which leaves `to` for its caller to delete when it fails after `to` exists), then commits v1; when fork_at or commit_refs fails, repository a-<to> stays (on a pruning host possibly still with the source's refs and objects) and a second fork to the same artifact answers `Repository a-<to> already exists`. Fix: delete `to` when a step after it exists fails (best effort), as GitContent::fork does, or let fork resume into an existing copy that has no v1.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"db4b2190206c372010808897ea41bbea0f1133ddbda0394044e2aaaea8a36ff9"},"summary":"A fork that fails after copying the repository leaves the copy, and the retry is refused","supersedes":"bed249c9ed40921d9cbf9a371a289d10f2bce2dd1bb49325cf3c20fabd63d9a5","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:38:24.036760Z","id":"88f9a2cd2868eef4b5a649b8a14dcf6e44b49a3f2b7228b122c3e1f98449d188","body":{"detail":"unpack() resolves the pack and links() parses each commit, tree and tag; unconnected() walks what a new ref value reaches and checks each link's type (a commit's tree a tree, its parents commits, a tree entry what its mode says, a tag's target its declared type). A pushed tree with an entry named .git, .., a duplicate name, unsorted entries, a non-UTF-8 name or a bad mode is still accepted and later served; git clients refuse such trees on checkout and git fsck --strict reports them. Fix: check trees as git fsck does (entry order, names, modes) and commits' header order before applying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":914},"end":{"line":983},"content_hash":"e19b7416387cc13c6fd38e81e5cdf49d1c0ca1931eae82dfc921ac126cea0012"},"summary":"Receive-pack checks that pushed objects parse, connect and have the type that names them, not the rest of what git's receive.fsckObjects checks","supersedes":"4ab81386db0b817ecab623392f37a6f1be2d6050d31b6bd375e04f0c87e29641","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053695Z","id":"1054e7c229c3ee034c0d7df7fc37fe6e0dd5925832664962784222c4d364f69e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6ff810dc09b9abec69aeb1697f695546e8a81b3434425be44c091b6bd4725e29","summary":"Since c3df54b3 a pushed v<n+1> that Artifacts accepts also blocks recording pushes: GitContent::tag_pushed (crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs:790:811) refuses when v<n> exists at another commit, so the reconcile fails on that commit and every later publish logs the failure and is refused by write_version. Syncing the tags as the prototype does (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts syncTags: move or delete v<digits> tags that name no version) would lift it.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139337Z","id":"c69b41ad0a635c3188a708cf8c2b9f6ee7b3c1dc2ce7095602ee0dac84c3de3d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ce995d14d1602576dbe9688b7beea116632367486f240599e74c301b82c89c1a","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/object.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139420Z","id":"f2ce5a49a9667be366e712d2d117474cbf1f497289809a13e7514827f1c3280b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ad3c5b2fec5d4e933a69c9dd84777b6f911e858f32407c0665f1148118002622","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139502Z","id":"ee054861c5461792efd7fbd1424153c5e4fd8bb6e23c8c9814febdef1fbaa70c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5846ac6a226ffa40aa13afff0f320bcbeba47f551ae02203dc426ce7f2b4fc2e","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/server.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139584Z","id":"ebd13325dd979ea7e8c5a1a837aafb59beceb2b4dc048a33bf236fda0edf9754","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"db4094c473ff8b01b79c07c7ac1d64a2424781fe1d3a5051ceef6aba462df6a8","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/pack.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372282Z","id":"fd70c280be5ea506db2d52884f65790f56238154154bb96de9fed5081e7fff72","body":{"detail":"parse_bounded has no limit on entries, and the stand-in's db::apply (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs apply) sums only the objects' data lengths against MAX_WRITE_BYTES. About a million distinct one-byte blobs fit a 12 MiB pack and a few MB unpacked, while RepoDO holds an entry, an offset-index slot, an ID and a cloned object per blob (well over 100 MB on wasm32, beside the isolate's other objects), and two rows per object push the write past the VFS's 16 MiB transaction cap (SQLITE_FULL, rolled back). Needs a write token.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"e7d667e8f1cb212d442c30689f3c744acb409c1d931f463b17afc8a500c93809"},"suggested_fix":"Add a max_objects bound to ReceiveOptions (about 50,000) checked as entries are parsed, and count a per-object overhead (about 64 bytes) in db::apply's byte total.","summary":"A pushed pack is bounded by bytes, not by object count: a 12 MiB pack of a million tiny blobs","tags":["security","worker","git","resource","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"fc092687a9552590688da0728dd73eb66b19b17f29a2c962a469dfdec4a396bb","body":{"detail":"What GitVersions reads from a commit is its tree, parents, message (trailers) and signatures: publish needs the parent's tree (versions.rs publish), read_file and list_files the version's tree, fork the source commit's tree, log the first-parent chain with messages. None needs the commit's raw bytes or recomputes its ID; the commit IDs come from refs. The binding's metadata carries exactly these. Re-encoding from metadata and checking the hash fails for commits people push (gpgsig, encoding, extra headers, other time zones), which are the ones the push reconcile reads. An upload-pack client is a negotiation plus a full pack per read from a Durable Object, for data the binding already answers. Since clax-core's store already holds each version's number, publisher and note, the git side is only the content and history. Shape: a Repo method such as read_commit_meta(id) -> Option<CommitMeta> whose default parses read_object (MemoryRepo and the stand-in keep working), overridden by the Artifacts repository from readCommit; GitVersions and tree.rs use it and read_object only for trees and blobs. The receive-pack client never sends a parent commit, so pushes are unaffected. This is needed before the Artifacts wiring, not before this crate merges.","kind":"comment","references":"f7f856c0ee767896292b1b48c64e6f7038a987fcf093ee0655b67987a9d62286","span":{"start":{"line":424},"end":{"line":430},"content_hash":"f4cab2018c684c3b3b635b1f9f9fb1dd0750392f2cd8f55482b4d4c588d1e5a8"},"summary":"Recommendation: give GitVersions a commit-metadata read path; neither re-encode commits nor fetch over upload-pack","supersedes":"9b2a74fcded82737bb5a203dbb0f88829ac4dc8f1bf934f4fd99ecaab6136a1b","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-git/src/pack.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T14:38:11.314412Z","id":"1100b8e852adee39fdc723b0e3b5c44d7f8728358f98cd31eb61c92727984ab5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d0598f46","summary":"Fixed in d0598f46: ReceiveOptions::max_objects (DEFAULT_MAX_OBJECTS 50,000) refuses a pack whose header declares more entries before any is read (ParsedPack::parse_within), and the stand-in's db::apply counts OBJECT_ROW_BYTES (64) per object against MAX_WRITE_BYTES. cargo test -p clax-git a_push_of_more_objects_than_the_limit_is_refused_at_unpack: 1 passed; (cd crates/clax-worker && cargo test many_tiny_objects_count_their_rows_against_the_bound): 1 passed; clax-git and clax-worker suites pass.","supersedes":"fd70c280be5ea506db2d52884f65790f56238154154bb96de9fed5081e7fff72","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
